  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Record the unit-interval values",
      "body": "<p>The given rule says the integrals on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow></math> are respectively <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>.</p>",
      "recap": "Integrals over adjacent intervals add to the integral over their union.",
      "pitfall": "The integer <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></math> is the lower endpoint; the value is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>.",
      "pause": "Build each forward integral to the common upper endpoint 3.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l21",
          "reminder": "Integrals over adjacent intervals add to the integral over their union."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Respect the order of the bounds",
      "body": "For a requested integral whose upper bound is smaller than its lower bound, reverse the bounds and attach a minus sign. Split forward integrals into the unit intervals from the rule.",
      "recap": "Reversing integration limits changes the sign; adjacent intervals add.",
      "pitfall": "Keep repeated contributions when different requested intervals overlap.",
      "pause": "Build all five signed integrals yourself and add their values.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b3-l08",
          "reminder": "Reversing integration limits changes the sign; adjacent intervals add."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "solution": "<p>Splitting into unit intervals gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p>Reversing bounds gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msubsup><mo>&#x0222B;</mo><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></math>. Their sum is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>Answer C.</strong></p>",
